Suppose Assumptions \ref{as-1} and \ref{as-2} are valid, and that $a^*<+\infty$ holds. We have the following alternative:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Either for every $\lambda \geq 0$, $u^\lambda(t,\cdot)\to 0$ in $\mathrm{L}^1(0,+\infty)$,
    \item or there exists a unique $\lambda^*>0$ such that
    \[
        \lim_{t\to \infty} u^\lambda(t,\cdot) = \begin{cases}
