\begin{theorem}\label{Main}
    For each marking $i$, let 
    $\upalpha^{\max}_i = \max_j \upalpha_{ij}.$ Then 
    \[\langle d_1 H^{\upnu_1}, \dots, d_n H^{\upnu_n} 
    \rangle^{\PP^k \vert \partial \PP^k}_{0,\upalpha} \leq 
    d_1 \cdots d_n \binom{n-3+k-\upnu}{n-3}
    \left( \sum_{i=1}^n \upalpha^{\max}_i \right)^{n-3},\]
    where $\upnu$ is the maximal codimension of an insertion at a 
    marked point with no tangency to the boundary. In particular, 
    if one imposes a point constraint at such a point this binomial
    coefficient is 1. 
\end{theorem}

