ref_dict.thm:PPPisRamanujan:
\begin{theorem}[The PPP is Ramanujan]\label{thm:PPPisRamanujan} 
The $G$-action on the $L^2(\Omega,\mu)$, the foliation of the PPP, decomposes as a direct sum of the trivial representation and a countable sum of copies of the regular representation. As a consequence, the foliated Laplacian has spectrum 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:spectralgap}
  \spec(-\Delta_\Omega)= \{0\} \cup \spec(-\Delta_G) = \{0\} \cup \left[\frac{(d-1)^2}{4}, \infty\right).  
\end{equation}
The bottom eigenvalue is simple and associated with the constant function $\mathbf 1_{\Omega}$.
\end{theorem}

